{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DONE — merged to main. Gerrit 1497 (`63db6ac5a8`) + follow-up 1499 (`52064a9ae7`), both LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1.\n\nDESIGN NOTE the plan surfaced: `transition` already had a valueless `--force` (start-work / plan-review gate bypass) distinct from `--force-close` (close gate). So this was not a pure rename — it is a COLLAPSE of two flags into one `--force[=<reason>]` that bypasses whichever gate the transition would hit, dispatched by target status. No dispatch ambiguity is introduced: on a close the valueless `--force` was already parsed and then discarded (`force` is read only on the start-work path), so no existing invocation changes meaning except by gaining the bypass it asked for by name. A bare `--force` on a close now records `(no reason given)`, matching `claim`.\n\nREJECTION, not silent skip — the load-bearing detail. `_parse_flags` is a hand-rolled loop that SILENTLY SKIPS unknown tokens, so deleting the flag would have made a stale `--force-close=\"reason\"` a silent no-op closing straight through the gate it meant to bypass. The retired spelling is matched explicitly and raises a CommandError naming `--force`. Token comparison is exact, so truncations stay unknown tokens rather than abbreviation-matching onto a live flag. 424f was still `open` at implementation time; this is complementary to its `allow_abbrev=False` work (that targets the argparse-based commands; `transition` does not use argparse), not in conflict with it.\n\nSCOPE decision: the library kwarg `rebar.transition(..., force_close=...)` and the internal `force_close` identifiers keep their names — the ticket renames the CLI flag string only. `transition_compute` gained a `force_reason` keyword so an explicit `--force=<reason>` becomes the start-work audit note, falling back to `--reason` text; `--force --reason=x` is unchanged. The reason propagates through the parent-first cascade.\n\nEXEMPTED from the rename: the three frozen `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/*.jsonl` corpora — recorded LLM-experiment input; rewriting them would corrupt the record. Everything else migrated, including `docs/adr/0043` (it names the live escape hatch, so it was updated in place rather than exempted).\n\nFOLLOW-UP 1499: bug e7a9's secret-screen override landed concurrently with a comment citing `--force-close=` as its flag-shape model. Caught post-merge and fixed so the tree-wide grep is genuinely clean.\n\nVERIFIED ON MAIN: tree-wide grep clean outside CHANGELOG / release-notes / the parser's rejection message and its test; `gen_cli_reference.py --check` passes; new `tests/unit/test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py` (12 tests) passes; full suite green apart from the pre-existing `test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py::test_live_clone` failure (reproduced on clean origin/main, unrelated — external jscpd tool). Complexity baseline drained (`_parse_flags` 18 -> 17). CHANGELOG breaking-change entry + `docs/release-notes.md` contract note added. MCP has no force bypass (unchanged)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786107737807495001,"uuid":"3c69e710-5cf6-4a4e-ae65-4ae7aa6071f2"}